    {
      "name": "3. IVR - Flow",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "3.1 Create Flow (sample provider-lookup test flow)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }, { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Smoke Test Flow\",\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"client_id\": \"welcome\",\n      \"type\": \"play\",\n      \"is_start\": true,\n      \"prompt_id\": \"{{prompt_welcome}}\",\n      \"next\": \"menu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"client_id\": \"menu\",\n      \"type\": \"menu\",\n      \"prompt_id\": \"{{prompt_menu}}\",\n      \"config\": { \"digit_timeout_ms\": 8000 },\n      \"branches\": { \"1\": \"collect_provider\", \"9\": \"hangup_node\" }\n    },\n    {\n      \"client_id\": \"collect_provider\",\n      \"type\": \"collect_input\",\n      \"prompt_id\": \"{{prompt_collect}}\",\n      \"config\": { \"max_digits\": 10, \"min_digits\": 10, \"terminator\": \"#\", \"store_as\": \"provider_number\" },\n      \"next\": \"lookup_provider\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"client_id\": \"lookup_provider\",\n      \"type\": \"lookup\",\n      \"config\": { \"source_type\": \"table\", \"table_id\": \"{{lookup_table_id}}\", \"lookup_key\": \"provider_number\", \"response_var_prefix\": \"provider_\" },\n      \"branches\": { \"found\": \"speak_result\", \"not_found\": \"not_found_node\" }\n    },\n    {\n      \"client_id\": \"speak_result\",\n      \"type\": \"play\",\n      \"prompt_id\": \"Your provider is {{provider_name}}. Thank you for calling.\",\n      \"next\": \"hangup_node\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"client_id\": \"not_found_node\",\n      \"type\": \"play\",\n      \"prompt_id\": \"{{prompt_notfound}}\",\n      \"next\": \"hangup_node\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"client_id\": \"hangup_node\",\n      \"type\": \"hangup\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ivr/flows", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "ivr", "flows"] },
            "description": "Exercises every node type relevant to your ask in one small flow: play, menu with real DTMF branching (1 -> lookup, 9 -> hangup), collect_input (full number entry), lookup against the hosted table, a dynamic branch on found/not_found, and a TTS-spoken prompt ('Your provider is {{'{{'}}provider_name{{'}}'}}...') that only gets synthesized at call time via Piper. IMPORTANT: {{'{{'}}provider_name{{'}}'}} in speak_result's prompt_id is NOT a Postman variable - leave it exactly as-is, it's a flow-engine template substituted live from the lookup result. This is a sample/test flow only; build your real flows the same way with your own content."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Flow created', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.id).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('flow_id', json.id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3.2 Get Flow",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ivr/flows/{{flow_id}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "ivr", "flows", "{{flow_id}}"] },
            "description": "Reads the flow back - confirms all 7 nodes and their branches persisted correctly, with client_id references resolved to real DB UUIDs."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Flow has all 7 nodes', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.nodes.length).to.eql(7);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Campaign",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "4.1 Create Broadcast Campaign (linked to the IVR flow)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                { "key": "name", "type": "text", "value": "Postman Test Campaign" },
                { "key": "phoneNumbers", "type": "text", "value": "[\"{{test_phone_number}}\"]" },
                { "key": "ivrFlowId", "type": "text", "value": "{{flow_id}}" }
              ]
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/campaigns/broadcast", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "campaigns", "broadcast"] },
            "description": "Requires login now (Workstream 9) and gets scoped to the caller's own tenant - previously zero-auth, which meant every campaign landed under one shared default tenant regardless of who created it. REPLACE {{test_phone_number}} (collection variable, currently a placeholder) with your own real number before running the collection if you want this to actually ring your phone once the gateway is back online. ivrFlowId links the campaign to the flow in the SAME insert as campaign creation - passing it up front (rather than a separate activate call afterward) closes a real race: the worker polls every 2s and can claim a 'pending' lead before a later link call takes effect, dispatching it through the plain audio_url path instead of the IVR engine. No audio file is needed here since the flow supplies its own prompts."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Campaign created', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.campaignId).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('campaign_id', json.campaignId);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4.2 List Campaigns",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/campaigns", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "campaigns"] },
            "description": "Requires login now (Workstream 9) - only shows campaigns belonging to the caller's own tenant."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Campaign list returned', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. IVR - Activate & Link Campaign",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "5.1 Mark Flow Active",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }, { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"campaignId\": \"{{campaign_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ivr/flows/{{flow_id}}/activate",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "ivr", "flows", "{{flow_id}}", "activate"]
            },
            "description": "The campaign is already linked to this flow (set atomically in step 4.1's ivrFlowId, closing the dispatch race a separate link-after-creation call would have). This step just marks the flow's own is_active flag true - re-sending campaignId here is harmless/idempotent, not what actually creates the link."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Flow activated and linked', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.is_active).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(json.campaignId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('campaign_id'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5.2 Verify Campaign Report Shows ivr_flow_id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/campaigns/{{campaign_id}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "campaigns", "{{campaign_id}}"] },
            "description": "Final proof the whole chain wired together correctly: campaign.ivr_flow_id should equal the flow_id from step 3.1. Once the Dinstar gateway is back online, the worker will dispatch this campaign's lead(s) through the IVR flow automatically - no further API calls needed."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Campaign is linked to the IVR flow', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.campaign.ivr_flow_id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('flow_id'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Agent & Calls (optional, Workstream 7)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "6.1 Create Test Agent",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }, { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{agent_username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{agent_password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/agents", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "agents"] },
            "description": "Creates a fresh test agent (rather than reusing the existing seeded agent1) and lazily provisions its SIP endpoint. If this username already exists from a previous run, you'll get a 409 - that's fine, just skip to 6.2."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('agent_id', json.agent.id);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Agent created or already exists', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.2 Agent Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{agent_username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{agent_password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "login"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Agent login succeeded', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('agent_token', json.token);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('agent_id', json.user.id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.3 Get My SIP Credentials",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{agent_token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me/sip-credentials", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "me", "sip-credentials"] },
            "description": "Returns { sipUsername, sipPassword, wssUrl } for the WebRTC softphone at /agent-softphone/."
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('SIP credentials returned', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.4 Agent Go Ready",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{agent_token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/calls/ready", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "calls", "ready"] },
            "description": "Moves the agent from 'login' to 'idle' - without this they're never eligible for the campaign_agents queue or inbound ACD."
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('Agent is idle', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.5 Agent Click-to-Dial",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }, { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{agent_token}}" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
